<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sanctuary of Asclepius at Epidaurus</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Asclepieion of Epidaurus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sanctuary of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asclepius">Asclepius</a> at Epidaurus, in the north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>, was the most celebrated healing centre of the ancient Greek world. From the late 5th century BCE the sick came to sleep in its halls hoping for healing dreams, and inscriptions record their cures. Its buildings include a temple, the tholos and a famous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a>, and it is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p></div>
